t-in voltage of <em>V<sub>D</sub></em> = 0.6 volt. If both the diodes are ON then which of the following statements are true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d5da1225d2b1baf33c029fbf3c5d30a594dfa2b5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/235eb47b62b5510d5c01e95ffb0e4ec81db232d4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/341703dc1758fcb0f867834435feb69332cc4f44.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/9f3361804cdad60c612596118c084246e0f67499.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/974ab7945707161e02443a90b91c8c54c34ebe68.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n In a JFET amplifier circuit shown below, the drain current changes from 4 mA to 8 mA and the gate voltage is changed from –3.8 volts to –3.3 volts in the current. The voltage gain of the amplifier is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d556dbddab772524b689e23e5816666ff40e6ccd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> –10</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> –8</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> –16</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> –4</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/e96f9799ecce40d0c429997c5d00dee8e66665bb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Assuming that the diodes in the circuit given are ideal,</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/018a591b1889158d8507ac0d9da9d9dd433cbc61.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n the voltage <em>V<sub>0</sub></em> is ________ V.</p></div>\n<di